:"the comparison reversed, never by negating, so unsigned weights work. Among equal weights"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the earlier position wins, as for the minimum; edges are listed in nonincreasing weight."}],"url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumspanningtree(weight:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumSpanningTree(weight:)"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/boruvkaMinimumSpanningTree(weight:)":{"title":"boruvkaMinimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Borůvka’s algorithm (JGraphT’s "},{"code":"BoruvkaMinimumSpanningTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX’s "},{"code":"'boruvka'","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each round every component takes its lightest edge to another component, under the strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (weight, position), so a round cannot close a cycle. The canonical minimum spanning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest of "},{"code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the same edges as Kruskal’s, listed by round and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an unspecified order within a round."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/boruvkaMinimumSpanningTree(weight:)","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/boruvkaminimumspanningtree(weight:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"boruvkaMinimumSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},